KNOWNBUG libcxx
main.cpp
--cpp11 --object-bits 12 --stdlib libc++ --unwind 4 --unwindset __builtin_memchr.0:27,__builtin_strlen.0:9 --unwinding-assertions
^\[main\.assertion\.1\] line \d+ 42: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.2\] line \d+ -7: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.3\] line \d+ x is no integer: SUCCESS$
^\[main\.assertion\.4\] line \d+ WRONG \(must FAIL\): FAILURE$
^\*\* 1 of \d+ failed
^VERIFICATION FAILED$
^EXIT=10$
^SIGNAL=0$
--
^warning: ignoring
unwinding assertion loop \d+: FAILURE
--
With libc++, num_get's facets and conversions had no models (cin.fail()
held on every path), its ctype<char>::do_widen loop needed 27 iterations,
and a pointer comparison with null in stringbuf::underflow was left
symbolic, which made the program too big to verify.
